MSDOS is not a multi-user system. UNIX is. When you're playing under
UNIX, you'll have to specify at compile-time what user is allowed to
use the -D option.

No other user can become a wizard when playing under UNIX, contrary to
when you're playing under MSDOS. When you're a non-wizard, you can't
use the -W option on a UNIX system. Period.

